###Block: Descriptions
Animate with the Spirit.MOD	DESC:Requests a spirit of a good aligned outsider to inhabit a corpse (6 HD max). This then fights for you. Summoning the spirit drains you of 1d3 points of Strength.
Benign Projection.MOD	DESC:You create an image of you that can shed light as a candle. It can only mimic your actions and speech, but you can cast spells with it from the abjuration, divination, and conjuration (healing) schools. Creating it drains you of 1d2 points of Strength.
Celestial Fortress.MOD	DESC:Creates a simple flat-roofed fort with a sturdy door, fireplace, but no windows. It is protected by consecrate and magic circle against evil. Creating it drains you of 1d2 points of Constitution.
Create Lantern Archon.MOD	DESC:Creates one new lantern archon in service of your patron deity. It will be friendly to you, but not under your control. It will perform 1 nonhazardous task of your choice for up to 1 hour without payment. Creating it will drain you of 1d2 points of Constitution.
Dawnshroud.MOD	DESC:Acts as a daylight spell, harms oozes and undead, each round they take 1d6 out to 60 ft or 1 point out to 120 ft. If the target touches a subject creature, they take 1d6+(min(CASTERLEVEL,15)) points of damage.
Disk of Solar Vengeance.MOD	DESC:This spell creates a disk of flame behind your head. It gives you Resistance to Cold 5 and any creature that strikes you without a reach weapon takes 1d6+(MIN(CASTERLEVEL,5)) points of fire damage. This discharages the spell. You can also discharge the spell willingly as a touch attack.
Dispel Silence.MOD	DESC:This spell dispels a silence effect. While you have it prepared, you get a +2 on Listen checks.
Eilistraee's Moonfire.MOD	DESC:You can use the moonfire as a melee touch attack that deals 2d6 of cold damage +(max(CASTERLEVEL,5)) or use it to spawn a (CASTERLEVEL) minute dancing lights spell.
Favor of Tymora.MOD	DESC:The target creature gets a +2 luck bonus to AC.
Faith Healing Wand.MOD	DESC:Temporarily changes any wand into a wand of faith healing with the same number of charges.
Fleeting Fortune.MOD	DESC:The target gets a +5 luck bonus on a single skill check of her choice.
Golden Dragonmail.MOD	DESC:Creates a suit of shining golden full plate (treat as +1 mithral full plate for arcane spell failure and AC). If you are a sorcerer, you also benefit from Res to Fire 10.
Holy Fire Shield.MOD	DESC:Creatures attacking you take fire or cold damage, with 1/2 being divine energy like the flame strike spell. Casting this gives you 1d3 points of Strength damage.
Love Bite.MOD	DESC:You choose either Fleeting Kiss (The target feels a kiss, which is used as a signal) or Love Bite (The target takes 1 pt of damage). This can be used to deliver a held touch spell at range by making the touch attack with a +2 bonus.
Portal Well.MOD	DESC:You create an extradimensional space in an active portal that you can hide in for the duration by entering the portal.
Rend Shadow Weave.MOD	DESC:Creates a zone of dead magic for the Shadow Weave. While you have this spell prepared, you get a +2 competence bonus on caster level checks to dispel Shadow Weave effects.
Ruinic Marker.MOD	DESC:You create a slender stone pillar 2 ft in diameter and 6 ft tall in the shape of your choice. You can inscribe up to 25 words on it. It also bears of glyph of warding (blast) that you can set to activate as you desire. When it activates, the marker is destroyed. This spell uses 1 vial of holy water.
Shard Blessing Aura.MOD	DESC:Aura creates lesser globe of invulnerability. If you are a sorcerer with Selune with you patron you also benefit from Protection from evil.
Silver Dragonmail.MOD	DESC:Creates a suit of +1 mithral breastplate on you with which you are proficient. Arcane spell failure and armor check penalties still apply. This has no affect if you were already wearing armor. If you are a sorcerer, this also gives you Cold Resistance 5.
Skin of the Steel Dragon.MOD	DESC:Grants you spell resistance of (CASTERLEVEL+10). If you are a sorcerer you also gain +5 on saves vs. poison.
Spellsong.MOD	DESC:When you cast this spell you immediately prepare one spell of 4th level or lower in this slot. As with other bard spells this does not work with Silent Spell.
Spellsong (Lesser).MOD	DESC:When you cast this spell you immediately prepare one spell of 1st level or lower in this slot. As with other bard spells this does not work with Silent Spell.
Spiderbind.MOD	DESC:Affected creatures are affected as a slow spell, reduced to one move or attack action during the round. Additionally, they take a -1 penalty on attack rolls, AC, and Reflex saves. They move at half their normal speed rounded down. Their poison attacks don't work for the duration. While the spell is prepared, you get a +2 circumstance save bonus against poison.
Stars of Mystra.MOD	DESC:Create (min(CASTERLEVEL/3,5)) stars that orbit your head like ioun stones. As a swift action you can launch 1 star at a target as a RTA. Each evil creature struck must make a save or lose a prepared spell or spell slot of level 4 or the highest lower level slot available determined randomly.
Stars of Selune.MOD	DESC:Create (min(CASTERLEVEL/3,5)) stars that orbit your head like ioun stones. As a swift action you can launch 1 star at a target as a RTA. Each star deals 1d8 of force and 1d8 of cold damage to the target.
Stormvoice.MOD	DESC:You voice is amplified. Subtract 10 from the DC of Listen checks made to hear you. You also gain a +2 competence bonus on Intimidate. While the spell is active, you can make a swift action to create a 15-foot-long cone-shaped burst with a shout. Targets take 1d8 points of sonic damage and make a Fortitude save or be stunned for 1 round. Doing so discharges the spell. Creatures that cannot hear are not stunned but still take the damage.
Thunderstroke.MOD	DESC:You call down a bolt of electricity that unerringly strikes your target dealing (min(CASTERLEVEL,5))d6. A small rumble of thunder accompanies the bolt, which is as loud as a battle (LISTEND DC -10 to hear).
Vision of Punishment.MOD	DESC:You give a target a vision of what awaits it in the afterlife. For most evil creatures this is a gut-wrenching vision. The target is nauseated if it fails its save, otherwise, it is sickened. The caster takes 1d2 points of Strength damage.

